  {
    "name": "system-scope",
    "text": "Zynq-7020 combines sound sensing and pointing. PL handles synchronous capture, frequency-domain correlation and pan–tilt PWM; PS handles 3D estimation, speaker verification and tracking. The final design adds local RGB touch control and direction-guided audio.",
    "x": 28,
    "y": 402,
    "w": 377,
    "h": 96,
    "size": 14.667
  },
  {
    "name": "technical-heading",
    "text": "Key technical challenges and design choices",
    "x": 28,
    "y": 508,
    "w": 377,
    "h": 25,
    "size": 14.667
  },
  {
    "name": "technical-body",
    "text": "3D direction: Non-coplanar mics constrain azimuth and elevation; no distance estimate.\nScheduling: Direction updates continue during speaker scoring. Passing results grant a timed permit.\nMotion: Direction quality, limits and mode gate motion. Axes default off, with stop and timeout guards.\nIntegration: Directional audio uses PCM and direction; touch links settings and status.",
    "x": 28,
    "y": 537,
    "w": 382,
    "h": 157,
    "size": 14.667
  },
